  "scope": "Proves the actual first-to-second Wilson locality bridge and physical contact repair through two genuine induced laws. First-block elimination produces explicitly computed local negative-log potentials on residual plaquettes and retained link stars, with factor supports at most 18. The normalized actual plaquette response depends on at most 18 retained links. A star-separated second block has a derived conditional product law under the actual induced action; a maximal packing proves such a block occupies at least 1/577 of surviving coordinates. Actual second removed covariance coefficients satisfy |C2|<=4 and vanish for disjoint response supports. Their literal periodic physical interpolation has amplitude4/a^8 and range10a inside the no-wrap pair ball2R+5a<n*a. A generic variable-range Taylor/tail theorem constructs continuous linear diagonal contacts and is applied to this actual kernel, including all periodic images. On a=(k+1)^-8,n=4(k+1)^9,R=k+1,m=72, second-stage local and tail errors decay as R^-4 and R^-8 for arbitrary couplings. Exact cell pairing and covariance telescoping prove a^-8 Cov_original-contact1-contact2=a^-8 Cov_twice_retained+o(1) on every real Schwartz tensor; separated covariances agree asymptotically. Variance-weighted local all-order moments and log-MGF estimates survive a genuine prior elimination. These finite-step statements neither give cutoff-independent physical all-order bounds nor prove bracket signs, a nonzero continuum theory or the mass gap.",
  "actual_induced_construction": {
    "action": "Independent first-block integration explicitly generates residual plaquette factors and negative-log single-link partition factors on retained stars. Their sum is the actual evolved action and yields the actual first marginal.",
    "support": "Generated factors and actual normalized plaquette responses have at most 18 retained coordinates. No closure in the original Wilson action family is assumed.",
    "second_product_law": "A next block with pairwise disjoint original link stars meets each generated factor in at most one coordinate; this proves its actual conditional product law.",
    "existence": "A maximal separated packing in the surviving edge inventory gives survivor.card<=577*T.card. It is nonempty if any survivor exists. The bound comes from star.card<=24 and closed conflicts of size <= 1+24^2.",
    "scope": "This is a finite first-to-second construction. It supplies neither a small generated interaction norm nor uniform support, density or contraction through an unbounded number of steps."
  },
  "second_removed_covariance": {
    "definition": "C2(p,q)=E_firstMarginal[(m_p-E[m_p|second exterior])*(m_q-E[m_q|second exterior])], with m_p the actual first response.",
    "amplitude": "The actual responses lie in[0,4]; the proved interval covariance bound yields |C2|<=4. C2 is symmetric and positive semidefinite.",
    "locality": "Actual second product independence gives C2=0 for disjoint response supports. Overlap implies physical sample distance<=10a when2R+5a<n*a.",
    "physical": "K2_a(x,y)=a^-8*C2(sample x,sample y) is measurable, globally bounded by4/a^8 and identified exactly with physical finite-cell sources, including periodic aliases."
  },
  "two_stage_schwartz_repair": {
    "contact": "The second contact integrates the degree-four relative-coordinate diagonal jet against the actual kernel truncated to |x|,|y|<=R and |x-y|<=12a. It is a continuous complex-linear Schwartz functional supported on the diagonal.",
    "estimate": "Second-stage error<=C2*p05(F)*a*R^4+4*weightedMoment_m(F)/(a^8*R^m), with C2=mass(4,3,1)*12^5/24. All periodic tails are included.",
    "path": "a=(k+1)^-8,n=4(k+1)^9,R=k+1,m=72; actual stronger no-wrap holds for k>=2. Local error is O(R^-4), tail O(R^-8), uniformly over beta and admissible blocks for each fixed Schwartz test.",
    "physical_identity": "a^-8 Cov_original-contact_first-contact_second=a^-8 Cov_twice_retained+o(1), for every real Schwartz tensor. Both removed covariance laws are the genuine successive laws.",
    "separated": "Diagonal-disjoint tensor support annihilates both contacts, so full and twice-retained physical separated covariances differ by o(1). No limit existence or nonzero value is inferred."
  },
  "variance_weighted_local_bounds": {
    "moments": "E|eta|^(k+2)<=L^k E[eta^2]; actual centered conditional moments satisfy the corresponding bound with L the original source interval width.",
    "log_mgf": "0<=log E exp(t eta)<=t^2 E[eta^2] for |t|L<=1. Actual first conditional responses inherit the same interval, so the next-stage law satisfies the same form.",
    "bare_plaquette": "L=4, giving |conditional moment(k+2)|<=4^k v and |conditional fourth cumulant|<=16v, uniformly in beta, volume and exterior.",
    "physical_limitation": "A physical source width can scale as 4a^-4||f||L1, so these bounds may grow with the cutoff and the controlled source radius may shrink like a^4. They do not provide uniform physical all-order jets or signs."
  },
  "remaining": [
    "Bound the final retained interacting covariance and establish a nonzero separated reflected signal and actual logarithmic bracket signs. The two removed contact remainders do not bound the retained physical covariance.",
    "Extend the proved first-to-second induced locality construction to a number of eliminations growing with the cutoff, controlling support growth, generated interaction norms, and summable contact errors. An extensive admissible second block and two-stage full-Schwartz subtraction are now proved, but uniform repeated-scale control is not.",
    "Control retained/noise mixed cumulants and higher partial-diagonal subtractions uniformly after physical source scaling. The variance-weighted all-order local moment and log-MGF estimates inherit the source interval width; physical source widths can grow like a^-4, so they are not cutoff-independent all-order correlation bounds.",
    "Construct the full compatible Schwinger hierarchy with reflection positivity, reflection and translation covariance, locality and all required field symmetries. The two constructed diagonal contact functionals have fixed-cutoff continuity, but their full symmetry/positivity compatibility is not proved.",
    "Establish the physical coupling trajectory, nonzero continuum normalization, relative physical transfer-energy control, field domains/cyclicity/spectrum, and every compact simple gauge group. All twelve full Clay requirements remain open."
  ],
